From 66c46a2c25487dcd42d765d7007d6a5ad5dd8e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:52:21 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/32] kcm_plasmasearch: runner list filled off the first
 frame (worker-thread scan, two-step model fill)

Page type: List (docs/page-design.md). krunnerrc keys, plugin ids, favorites order, config dialogs and D-Bus
notifications are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- The usage paragraph above the list became a Kirigami.ContextualHelpButton beside the search field, same text
  (kcm_plasmasearch/SearchField). The page opens with the search field and the list.
- Page actions: Configure KRunner... and Get New Plugins... kept; new links "File Search Settings..." (kcm_baloofile)
  and "Web Search Keywords..." (kcm_webshortcuts) through KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings. Per ia/duplicates.md this
  page owns the baloosearchEnabled runner switch (the per-runner checkbox stays here); kcm_baloofile still writes the
  key on save (kcms/baloo/kcm.cpp:92-96), which I did not touch (other page, behaviour change: manager decides).
- Busy indicator appears only after 150 ms of loading (kcm.loading property, new).
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_plasmasearch.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 22 rows ok, 1 reported lost
  (kcm_plasmasearch/list, Special Characters list in kdeplasma-addons/runners/characters/charrunner_config.ui: not
  part of this page's files, untouched).

Speed (cause from code, not measured):
- SearchConfigModule::load() called reloadPlugins() synchronously, which ran RunnerManager::runnerMetaDataList()
  (scans the kf6/krunner plugin dirs and parses every runner's metadata, plus D-Bus runner desktop files) and then
  KPluginModel::addPlugins() for all ~21 runners; addPlugins calls findConfig() per plugin, a QPluginLoader probe for
  each X-KDE-ConfigModule (kcmutils/src/core/kpluginmodel.cpp:42-61, 190-204). All of it before the first frame.
- Now the scan runs in a QThread (QThread::create, Qt Core only) and the result is cached, so Reset reuses it and
  only Get New Plugins rescans. The model is filled in two steps: favorites (4 by default), then, one event-loop turn
  later, the rest. Stale fills (Reset/Defaults while loading) are dropped by a generation counter. Defaults applies
  KPluginModel::defaults() after the fill completes.
- Numbers: before (build/bench/clean/before-*.tsv, measured under load) fast 487-1116 ms first run, slow (0.5 CPU)
  2114-2261 ms. After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-019, HIG-020, HIG-047, HIG-058.

Not built yet (freeze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
